{"headword":"יְהוֹשָׁפָט","parent_lexicon":"BDB Dictionary","content":{"senses":[{"definition":"<strong>n.pr.m.</strong> 𝔊 Ἰωσαφαω, Ἰωσαφατ <strong>(</strong><span dir=\"rtl\">י׳</span> <em>hath judged</em>, cf. <a data-ref=\"BDB, אֱלִישָׁפָט\" href=\"/BDB,_אֱלִישָׁפָט\", dir=\"rtl\">אֱלִישָׁפָט</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">שְׁפַטְיָהוּ</span> & reff.<strong>)</strong>—"},{"senses":[{"definition":"<span dir=\"rtl\">יְהוֹ׳</span> (so all except <strong>5.</strong> & <strong>6</strong>) king of Judah, son of Asa <a data-ref=\"I Kings 15:24\" href=\"/I_Kings.15.24\">1 K 15:24</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Kings 22:2\" href=\"/I_Kings.22.2\">22:2</a> + 21 times 1 K; <a data-ref=\"II Kings 1:17\" href=\"/II_Kings.1.17\">2 K 1:17</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Kings 3:1\" href=\"/II_Kings.3.1\">3:1</a>, <a data-ref=\"II Kings 3:7\" href=\"/II_Kings.3.7\">7</a>, <a data-ref=\"II Kings 3:11\" href=\"/II_Kings.3.11\">11</a>, <a data-ref=\"II Kings 3:12\" href=\"/II_Kings.3.12\">12</a><sup>(×2)</sup>, <a data-ref=\"II Kings 3:14\" href=\"/II_Kings.3.14\">14</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Kings 8:16\" href=\"/II_Kings.8.16\">8:16</a><sup>(×2)</sup>, <a data-ref=\"II Kings 12:19\" href=\"/II_Kings.12.19\">12:19</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 3:10\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.3.10\">1 Ch 3:10</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 17:1\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.17.1\">2 Ch 17:1</a> + 40 times 2 Ch."}],"num":"1."},{"senses":[{"definition":"father of Jehu king of Israel <a data-ref=\"II Kings 9:2\" href=\"/II_Kings.9.2\">2 K 9:2</a>, <a data-ref=\"II Kings 9:14\" href=\"/II_Kings.9.14\">14</a>."}],"all_cited":true,"num":"2."},{"senses":[{"definition":"chronicler under David & Solomon, son of Ahilud <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 8:16\" href=\"/II_Samuel.8.16\">2 S 8:16</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Kings 4:3\" href=\"/I_Kings.4.3\">1 K 4:3</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 18:15\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.18.15\">1 Ch 18:15</a>; also <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 20:24\" href=\"/II_Samuel.20.24\">2 S 20:24</a> (𝔊L Σαφαν)."}],"all_cited":true,"num":"3."},{"senses":[{"definition":"one of Sol.’s 12 officers who provided victuals for the royal household <a data-ref=\"I Kings 4:17\" href=\"/I_Kings.4.17\">1 K 4:17</a> (𝔊L Ἰωασαφατ)."}],"all_cited":true,"num":"4."},{"senses":[{"definition":"<span dir=\"rtl\">יוֹ׳</span> one of David’s heroes <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 11:43\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.11.43\">1 Ch 11:43</a>."}],"all_cited":true,"num":"5."},{"senses":[{"definition":"<span dir=\"rtl\">יוֹ׳</span> a priest & trumpeter in David’s time <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 15:24\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.15.24\">1 Ch 15:24</a>."}],"all_cited":true,"num":"6."},{"senses":[{"definition":"in <strong>n.pr.loc.</strong> <span dir=\"rtl\">עֵמֶק יְהוֹשָׁפָט</span> <a data-ref=\"Joel 4:2\" href=\"/Joel.4.2\">Jo 4:2</a>, <a data-ref=\"Joel 4:12\" href=\"/Joel.4.12\">12</a>, symbolical name of a valley near Jerusalem, place of ultimate judgment."}],"all_cited":true,"num":"7."}]},"rid":"BDB02350","strong_numbers":["3092","3146"],"next_hw":"יוֹאָב","prev_hw":"יְהוֹשָׁמָע","alt_headwords":[{"word":"יוֹשָׁפָט"}],"quotes":[],"GK":["3398","3399","3461"],"TWOT":[],"parent_lexicon_details":{"name":"BDB Dictionary","language":"heb.biblical","to_language":"eng","text_categories":[],"source":"BDB Dictionary","attribution":"F. Brown, S. Driver & C. Briggs","index_title":"BDB","version_title":"A Hebrew and English lexicon of the Old Testament, by Francis Brown. With the co-operation of S. R. Driver and Charles A. Briggs. Oxford, 1906","version_lang":"en","should_autocomplete":true}}